  "id": "COMPOUND:42504 - PROTEIN:2333",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex network of interactions linking methyl (Z)-pentadec-8-enoate to Mono-ADP-ribosyltransferase C3 through multiple intermediate targets. The drug methyl (Z)-pentadec-8-enoate is identified as a target of several compounds, including 8-O-(P-Coumaroyl)-1(10)E,4(5)E-Humuladien-8-Ol and Conferol, which in turn target Mono-ADP-ribosyltransferase C3. This indicates that methyl (Z)-pentadec-8-enoate may exert its biological effects via these intermediates, potentially through a mechanism involving the modulation of enzyme activity. The presence of multiple pathways suggests that the drug may act through different molecular mechanisms, possibly involving the activation or inhibition of the target enzyme. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of the enzyme in the drug's biological action, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
